                <pb facs="0406" n="398" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg398"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/13803: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-08-16T19:00:00-04:00">August 16, 1941—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3182. Your 3511, August 8, 10 p.m. Please inform Mr. Eden that this Government
                    appreciates being informed of the nature of the memorandum to be delivered to
                    the Iranian Government, and that our Minister in Tehran has been informed of
                    this action.</p>
                <p>You may say to Mr. Eden that while we do not wish our Minister to participate in
                    the joint representations being made in Tehran, he will bear them in mind in his
                    conversations on this subject with the Iranian Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
